  "question": {
    "text": "Two objects are projected with same velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi></math>&nbsp;however at different angles&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;with the horizontal. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, the ratio of horizontal range of the first object to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>nd</mi></msup></math> object will be :",
    "image": null
  },
